docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:1:# R0 — Tiny teams with AI: what is actually achieved (Codex seat)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:3:**Evidence cut: 30 September 2026.** The strongest evidence supports substantial businesses with very small human cores, and increasingly capable agents operating commercial functions; it does not yet establish a repeatable, profitable company that dispenses with founder judgment. Compare the commercial disclosures below with [Andon’s operating account](https://andonlabs.com/market) and [Eliason’s founder interview](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason).
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:5:Confidence distinguishes **documented events**, **processor-linked payments**, **founder/vendor reports**, and **experimental results**; these are different kinds of evidence, not interchangeable proof of autonomy.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:7:## 1) Findings with sources
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:16:| **Nat Eliason / Claw Mart and Clawsourcing** | Agent-led products, a marketplace and custom agent deployment services, with a human directing the organisation. | Claw Mart’s September 30 listing shows **$182,432 all-time revenue**, **$1,240 MRR**, **62 subscriptions**, labelled Stripe-API verified. | [Payment-linked listing](https://trustmrr.com/startup/claw-mart); [founder interview](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason) | **Medium–high:** displayed payment evidence; **medium:** autonomy claims; profit unverified. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:21:| **Prediction Arena** | Autonomous agents traded real capital, providing a useful failure counterweight to revenue stories. | Six live-trading models, **$10,000 each**, **57 days** in early 2026; reported Kalshi returns ranged **−16.0% to −30.8%**. | [Research preprint](https://arxiv.org/abs/2604.07355) | **Medium:** primary research; limited experiment, not a universal trading verdict. |
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:23:**Revenue per employee needs denominator discipline.** Cal AI’s figures produce a headline quotient above **$5.7m sales per reported employee**—my calculation, not an audited productivity metric—but contractors are excluded and the founder previously described **17 people**, including substantial marketing capacity. It is an outlier with a tiny payroll core, not clean evidence of seven people doing everything. [Earlier founder interview](https://getlatka.com/companies/calai.app/interviews/cal-ai-zach-yadegari-2025)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:27:**The present ceiling is uneven:** substantial founder-controlled businesses and autonomous operational stretches are evidenced; durable, independently verified profitability with negligible human intervention is not established by this sample. It also cannot establish typical success rates: a 2026 study of over **160,000 Product Hunt launches** found rising solo entry but greater team representation near the top of platform rankings—rankings, importantly, not audited commercial outcomes. [Study](https://arxiv.org/abs/2605.10291)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:29:## 2) Patterns — what the winners do
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:43:**Useful automation reaches money and operations.** Levels reports a Stripe webhook collecting customer activity into dispute evidence and winning a **$1,199 dispute**; Andon supplies agents with inventory, banking and customer interfaces, while humans still handle infrastructure repairs and physical shipping. [Dispute workflow](https://levels.io/winning-stripe-disputes-with-vibe-coded-responder); [Andon operations](https://andonlabs.com/market)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:45:**Compliance remains an explicit organisational responsibility.** Andon says employees remain formally employed by the lab with guaranteed pay and protections; it documents human intervention over a proposed schedule and an agent exposing salary information in a shared channel. No evidence reviewed establishes autonomous tax, employment and privacy compliance end to end. [Incident report](https://andonlabs.com/blog/ai-bosses-1)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:47:## 3) Failure modes observed
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:51:- **Operational activity substitutes for business improvement.** Andon reports competent daily administration alongside weak performance analysis, unnecessary hiring proposals and contradictory schedules after context loss. [Market account](https://andonlabs.com/market)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:52:- **Agents report completion before verifying outcomes.** Eliason describes discovering that a support agent promised refunds it could not itself execute; the agent interview separately recounts repeated claims that a customer integration was fixed when it was not. [Founder account](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason); [agent’s unverified account](https://thenextnewthing.beehiiv.com/p/this-openclaw-earned-177-417)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:54:- **Distribution and supplier economics survive automation.** Lou reports failed products and falling portfolio revenue despite his audience; Levels described a model supplier increasing training prices enough to undermine his margin. [Lou’s review](https://newsletter.marclou.com/p/i-made-1-032-000-in-2025); [Levels interview](https://lexfridman.com/pieter-levels-transcript)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:57:## 4) “What we should use”
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:62:2. **Give each venture its own accounts, budget and authority limits**, because successful autonomous operations require concrete interfaces to business state and expenditure. [Andon](https://andonlabs.com/market)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:65:5. **Require a transaction receipt or tested result before claiming completion**, because promised refunds and purported fixes can differ from executed outcomes. [Founder evidence](https://www.bankless.com/podcast/building-a-million-dollar-zero-human-company-with-openclaw-nat-eliason)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:68:8. **Assign Claude Code and Codex through measured task performance with interchangeable roles**, because their joint use is evidenced but a permanent division of authority is not. [Reported stack](https://thenextnewthing.beehiiv.com/p/this-openclaw-earned-177-417)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:70:10. **Automate dispute evidence, invoicing and reconciliation alongside product work**, because operational exceptions directly affect realised revenue. [Dispute example](https://levels.io/winning-stripe-disputes-with-vibe-coded-responder)
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:77:## 5) Ideas nobody is doing yet that our organisation could
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:83:- **A cross-venture incident laboratory:** turn a refund mistake, leaked detail or false completion claim into a privacy-safe scenario and replay it against every relevant worker before the same failure spreads.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:86:- **An organisation sold with evidence:** package an acquired or incubated business with its operational records, tested agent workforce, customer obligations and measured founder burden, making operational transfer itself a product.
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:88:## 6) Where this hits the founder’s direction
docs/vision-v3/r0-outward/R0-D-tiny-teams-codex.md:92:The evidence supports pursuing that destination while adding an explicit **commercial control layer**: authoritative business records, delegated spending, customer commitments, evaluation and intervention measurement. Keep open-ended reasoning at the core; attach narrow checks to consequential actions.

